    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176">

                <pb facs="0266" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.60D11/505</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Finnish
                        Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Procopé</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-23">March 23, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of March 13, 1943<anchor n="35" xml:id="d176-f1"/>
                    concerning the recognition of Captain Holger Grondahl, newly appointed Military
                    Attaché at the Legation of Finland, to be also in charge of naval matters at the
                    Legation.</p>
                <p>A copy of the Minister’s note was referred to the Navy Department, and a reply
                    has now been received in which the Navy Department states as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In view of the Finnish Government’s agreement to accept an American
                            Naval Officer as Naval Attaché to the Legation at Helsinki with
                            residence there, in addition to the Assistant Naval Attaché accredited
                            to Finland but resident in Stockholm, the Navy Department agrees to the
                            acceptance of Captain Holger Grondahl to be in charge of naval matters
                            in Washington.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d176-f1" n="35" xml:id="d176-f1-content">
                <p>This note approved the request to appoint an American Naval Attaché to the United
                    States Legation in Finland and confirmed the view that the Finnish Government
                    desired to enlarge contact between the American and Finnish naval
                    establishments.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
